  "worked_solution": "We start by using the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}})}^{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{(3y)^{3}}{{({x}^{2})}^{3}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power of product rule in the numerator and the power rule in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(3y)^{3}}{{({x}^{2})}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{3}^{3}{y}^{3}}{{x}^{2\\cdot 3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{27{y}^{3}}{{x}^{6}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
